      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T05:20:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are the consequence of this change ?\ngoing from 5s to 100 ms looks like a huge step, I am worried about unwanted consequence of this change",
      "revId": "28aa7aa04a68abad92592ec5fa5bd148d3d343d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a5c2b8e_0f211823",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T20:29:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since Android T, LE scan window/interval 100ms/100ms for LOW_LATENCY has been used from ScanManager.java by aosp/2027383, but this change was not applied to native BT stack. In aosp/2027383 description, reducing interval/window could provide better scan performance, but the scan duty cycle is still 100%.\n\n```\nReduce low latency mode scan interval to 100ms for the better channel\ndiversity. Test results indicate there is no change of discovery\nlatency with the small scan interval in the home environment.\n```",
      "parentUuid": "4e15bd7e_525c0d61",
      "revId": "28aa7aa04a68abad92592ec5fa5bd148d3d343d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d2413df3_eba12eed",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T20:55:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does that mean that aosp/2027383 had no effect ? It mention that the values has been manually checked.\nIf this other CL had effect, then what the native value are used for and in which context ?\n\nIf they need to be kept in sync with the java, should we only defined the value once and make the java ask the native what the value is ? or the other way around, the native ask the java, as you prefer. (I prefer the first but)",
      "parentUuid": "7a5c2b8e_0f211823",
      "revId": "28aa7aa04a68abad92592ec5fa5bd148d3d343d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ff1b9d8_b4a8faa2",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1959861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T01:15:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Overall scan performance is same but 100ms/100ms could have better channel diversity because LE scan radio frequency is stuck during LE scan window. 5 seconds was too big. It seems your proposal to sync the parameters between framework and native stack is really good to have. I hope to the design could be done by another CL.",
      "parentUuid": "d2413df3_eba12eed",
      "revId": "28aa7aa04a68abad92592ec5fa5bd148d3d343d0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
